The West Four Wrestling Alliance is a longtime wrestling promotion in Manitoba, owned and operated by Tony Condello. The promotion is noted for helping to launch the careers of men like Lance Storm, Chris Jericho and Don Callis, as well as being the final stop for men like Baron von Raschke and Bob Brown.
